module_common: connect each DRM file once

Unless connecting is left to the PVR_SRVKM_INIT ioctl (PVRSRV_LINUX_DEV_INIT_ON_CONNECT; this
build uses ON_PROBE), pvr_drm_open() connects the file, and the user libraries' ioctl then
called PVRSRVDeviceServicesOpen() again, making a second connection that replaced the first.
Closing the file disconnected only the second, so the first stayed in the device's connection
list forever and kept its reference on the process's handle base (one per PID). That base, and
every handle in it (e.g. display buffer imports, which keep display contexts and their
"pvr_misr" threads alive), was then never freed. The ioctl now keeps the file's existing
connection. Found on the TrimUI Brick, 2026-10-18.

--- a/services/server/env/linux/module_common.c
+++ b/services/server/env/linux/module_common.c
@@ -542,6 +542,19 @@
 	else
 	{
 		psConnectionPriv = (PVRSRV_CONNECTION_PRIV*)psDRMFile->driver_priv;
+
+#if (PVRSRV_DEVICE_INIT_MODE != PVRSRV_LINUX_DEV_INIT_ON_CONNECT)
+		/* One connection per file: open() has already connected it, so the
+		 * user libraries' PVR_SRVKM_INIT ioctl must not connect again. A
+		 * second connection would replace the first, which would then never
+		 * be disconnected, nor its process's handle base freed.
+		 */
+		if (psConnectionPriv->pvConnectionData)
+		{
+			mutex_unlock(&sDeviceInitMutex);
+			goto out;
+		}
+#endif
 	}
 
 	if (psDeviceNode->eDevState == PVRSRV_DEVICE_STATE_CREATED)
